[[File:Comprehensive Laboratory Detective Pikachu.png|thumb|280px|A depiction of the lab from [[Detective Pikachu Ryme City Guide]]]]
The '''Pokémon Comprehensive Laboratory''' (Japanese: '''ポケモン{{tt|総合研究所|そうごうけんきゅうしょ}}''' ''Pokémon Comprehensive Laboratory''), or '''PCL''' (Japanese: '''{{j|PCL}}''' ''PCL'') for short, is a research facility in the game {{OBP|Detective Pikachu|video game}}. The laboratory is located on a mountain pass in east [[Ryme City]] in the district of East Highland<ref>[[Detective Pikachu Ryme City Guide]]</ref>. Scientists here research the abilities of Pokémon and have developed various inventions. 

PC was founded by [[John Waals]] over 20 years ago in an effort to improve the relationship between people and Pokémon. The lab was temporarily shut down ten years ago for two years due to damage caused by a berserk Pokémon. Contemporary researchers include [[Wallace Carroll]], [[Carlos Hernando]], [[Frederick Hartfield]], and [[Nina O'Hara]], with current director [[Dorothy Fisher]]. The compound is divided between Building A on the left and Building B on the right, with a courtyard between them.

[[Tim Goodman|Tim]] and [[Detective Pikachu (character)|Pikachu]] investigate PCL under the cover of working there as a part-time job. Most of Chapter 3 takes place here.

